docs/BACKEND_REVIEW.md:72:Measured actual Neo4j transactions: identical generation retry or repeated progress uses **10 integrity queries and zero materialization writes**; changed progress uses **12 queries**, including only its changed job and ledger. An unrelated five-revision history remains unchanged. Tampering with unrelated history still blocks a no-op retry without repair. API responses avoid duplicate ledger reads. Full locked graph-copy verification, whole-ledger serialization and ranking snapshots for exact active revision baselines remain deliberate prototype integrity costs; scalability is not established.
